---
// promptanddone.com/credentials: the CREDENTIALS pack (DM deliverable for the "chatgpt-image-credentials" reel).
import PackLayout from '../layouts/PackLayout.astro';
const script = `import sys, json, c2pa

for path in sys.argv[1:]:
    try:
        data = json.loads(c2pa.Reader(path).json())
        m = data["manifests"][data["active_manifest"]]
        acts = [a for a in m["assertions"] if a["label"].startswith("c2pa.actions")]
        act = acts[0]["data"]["actions"][0] if acts else {}
        sig = m["signature_info"]
        print(path, "CREDENTIALS FOUND", sig.get("issuer"), act.get("softwareAgent"), act.get("action"), str(act.get("digitalSourceType", "")).split("/")[-1], str(sig.get("time"))[:10], data.get("validation_state"))
    except Exception as e:
        print(path, "NO CREDENTIALS FOUND (that proves nothing about who made it)")`;
---
<PackLayout title="Check an image for Content Credentials — Prompt &amp; Done">
  <main>
    <header>
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/">Prompt &amp; Done</a> · CREDENTIALS pack</p>
      <h1>Does this image carry Content Credentials? The checker from the reel.</h1>
      <p class="tag">Content Credentials (C2PA) are signed metadata inside an image file: who issued it, which tool made it, whether it is AI-generated. They are optional, and they are easy to lose.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">1</span> The checker</h2>
      <pre><code>python3.11 -m venv v &amp;&amp; v/bin/pip install c2pa-python
v/bin/python check.py your-image.jpg</code></pre>
      <pre><code>{script}</code></pre>
      <p class="note">Tested 26 Oct 2026 with c2pa-python 0.38.1 on macOS. Reads a file and prints what is signed inside it; it does not detect AI by itself.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">2</span> What we ran in the reel (26 Oct 2026)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Original:</b> Adobe Firefly sample image (contentauth/example-assets). Credentials found: issuer Adobe Inc., tool Adobe Firefly, action c2pa.created, source trainedAlgorithmicMedia, signed 2025-10-23, validation Valid.</li>
        <li><b>Resized and re-saved as JPEG:</b> no credentials found.</li>
        <li><b>Re-saved as PNG:</b> no credentials found.</li>
        <li><b>Browser screenshot of the original:</b> no credentials found.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>One example, one tool. Not every export or screenshot method behaves the same, and some platforms keep or re-attach credentials.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">3</span> What OpenAI says</h2>
      <p>OpenAI's developer docs say its images can carry C2PA Content Credentials and a SynthID watermark, and that you can check a file at openai.com/verify. They also say: "Compression, cropping, screenshots, metadata removal, and format conversions can erase or weaken a signal." And on a "not detected" result: "Treat not_detected as an absence of detected evidence." It "doesn't rule out AI-generated or AI-modified content."</p>
      <p><a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/content-provenance">OpenAI developer docs: Content provenance</a></p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">4</span> Links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/contentauth/example-assets">Content Authenticity Initiative example assets</a> (the Firefly sample)</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/contentauth/c2pa-python">c2pa-python</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://openai.com/verify">openai.com/verify</a> (OpenAI's own checker)</li>
      </ul></section>
  </main>
</PackLayout>
